Package: rbFoFR
Type: Package
Title: Nonlinear Function-on-Function Regression from Fragments
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Ufuk", family = "Beyaztas",
    role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "ufuk.beyaztas@marmara.edu.tr",
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-5208-4950"))
Description: Estimation of the identifiable component of a nonlinear
    function-on-function regression operator when each predictor curve is
    observed only on a window of fixed length. The predictor is expanded in a
    known localized basis with independent symmetric scores, and the operator
    is a finite sum of products of scores (Walsh functionals) with
    function-valued coefficients. The package computes co-observation
    probabilities, the resolution order and the partition of interactions
    into estimated, trimmed and non-resolvable directions, and fits the
    resolvable coefficients by inverse-probability weighting or by a
    complete-case ratio estimator without reconstructing unobserved parts of
    the curves. Data generators for the seven simulation designs of the
    accompanying paper, Fisher information and risk benchmarks, and
    evaluation tools are included.
License: GPL (>= 2)
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
Imports: stats, utils
NeedsCompilation: no
